/**
 * Where to change nameservers, per registrar — FCS-081.
 * ============================================================================
 * Step 3 of the connect pipeline hands somebody two nameservers and sends
 * them to a website we do not control. That is the step the whole thing dies
 * at: the customer alt-tabs into GoDaddy, cannot find the setting, and the
 * domain never connects.
 *
 * ── WHY THE PATHS ARE WRITTEN LOOSELY ──────────────────────────────────────
 * Every registrar redesigns its dashboard, and a screenshot or a pixel-exact
 * path goes stale silently — worse than no instructions, because somebody
 * trusts it and concludes the feature is broken. So each entry names the
 * SEQUENCE OF LABELS to look for, which survives a redesign, and the screen
 * says in as many words that the wording may differ.
 *
 * ── AND WHY THERE IS A GENERIC ONE ─────────────────────────────────────────
 * There are hundreds of registrars. The last entry is the shape the job takes
 * everywhere, so somebody at a registrar nobody here has heard of is not left
 * with nothing.
 */

